I believe that after full matching one of the outputs will be a new "subclass" variable, which will show which subclasses people are in, which you could use for this purpose.  I believe you can get that subclass vector either as part of the matchit output or if you use the match.data() command it will be a new variable in the resulting data set.

Liz


On 10/22/12 7:19 AM, "Xin Yuan" <xin-yuan1989-PkbjNfxxIARBDgjK7y7TUQ at public.gmane.org> wrote:

Hi there,
I need to know who matched with who using full method. I can get the match.matrix when I use nearest, optimal, or other methods. But when I set the method as "full", the match.matrix I got was null. Do you know how to get that matched matrix?
All your help will be greatly appreciated.

Best,
Xin

